{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>So the daughters of Zelophehad speak.</b> As its Targum renders: 'יָאוּת' — thus is this passage written before Me on high; this teaches that the eye of the cloud saw what the eye of Moses did not see (Tanchuma)." "<b>So the daughters of Zelophehad speak.</b> They have claimed well. Happy is the man whom the Holy One, blessed be He, acknowledges in his words (Sifrei)." "<b>You shall surely give.</b> Two portions: the portion of their father, who was among those who left Egypt, and his portion with his brothers in the property of Hepher (Bava Batra 118)." "<b>And you shall transfer.</b> It is an expression of wrath, concerning one who does not leave a son to inherit him. Another interpretation — on account that a daughter transfers inheritance from tribe to tribe, for her son and husband inherit her — for 'לֹא תִסֹּב נַחֲלָה' (Numbers 36) was commanded only for that generation alone (Bava Batra 120) — and likewise ״וְהַעֲבַרְתֶּם אֶת נַחֲלָתוֹ לְבִתּוֹ״; in all of them it says 'וּנְתַתֶּם' but for the daughter it says 'וְהַעֲבַרְתֶּם'."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:03.348201528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}